### What is Flyway and how does it manage database migrations?

Flyway is a database migration tool that runs versioned SQL scripts on application startup. Each script has a version number (V1, V2, V3), and Flyway records which versions have been applied in the `flyway_schema_history` table. This ensures each migration runs exactly once, even across multiple deployments.

The critical rule is: never modify a migration after it has been applied. Always create a new version.

```text
Project structure:
src/main/resources/db/migration/
  V1__create_accounts_table.sql
  V2__add_balance_column.sql
  V3__create_transactions_table.sql
  V4__add_index_on_account_id.sql
```

```sql
-- V1__create_accounts_table.sql
CREATE TABLE accounts (
    id          VARCHAR(20) PRIMARY KEY,
    customer_id VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
    account_type VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL,
    status      VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'ACTIVE',
    created_at  TIMESTAMP   NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- V2__add_balance_column.sql
ALTER TABLE accounts ADD COLUMN balance DECIMAL(15,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.00;

-- V3__create_transactions_table.sql
CREATE TABLE transactions (
    id          VARCHAR(36) PRIMARY KEY,
    account_id  VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL REFERENCES accounts(id),
    amount      DECIMAL(15,2) NOT NULL,
    txn_type    VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL,
    description VARCHAR(200),
    created_at  TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);
```

